librsvg-c for Debian/Devuan
===========================

This source package is named **librsvg-c** so it does not collide with
GNOME/Rust **librsvg2** in the archive namespace.

The binaries displace/replaces the official librsvg2-* packages on the system.
They keep the same C API and SONAME **librsvg-2.so.2**:

  librsvg-c2        Conflicts/Replaces/Provides  librsvg2-2
  librsvg-c-common  Conflicts/Replaces/Provides  librsvg2-common
  librsvg-c-dev     Conflicts/Replaces/Provides  librsvg2-dev
  librsvg-c-bin     Conflicts/Replaces/Provides  librsvg2-bin

gir1.2-rsvg-2.0 is not shipped (introspection is disabled).

css/ is the only CSS engine. libcroco is not built or packaged.

`librsvg-c2` Depends on **libgif7** (GIF in SVG `<image>`).

After installing librsvg-c-common, postinst refreshes gdk-pixbuf
loaders.cache. After removal, postrm does the same so the SVG loader
is unregistered. The loader file is `libpixbufloader-svg.so` (hyphen).

Install (desktop)
-----------------

Install **all needed local debs in one apt transaction**:

    apt-get install -y ./librsvg-c2_*.deb ./librsvg-c-common_*.deb \
      ./librsvg-c-bin_*.deb ./librsvg-c-dev_*.deb

`c2` + `common` is the desktop atomic pair. `-dev` is optional.
Never `dpkg -i librsvg-c2` alone while GNOME librsvg2-common is
installed. Never `apt-get -f` after a failed replace of librsvg2-*:
apt will remove the half-unpacked C packages and can drop
desktop-base / icon themes.

Full guide: `deb/INSTALL.md` in the source tree (copied next to the
.debs as INSTALL.md when you run `make deb`).

Verify:

    dpkg -l | grep librsvg
    rsvg-convert --version
    gdk-pixbuf-query-loaders | grep svg
